{"id": "DfL_Jr9islH", "title": "Video by feartalkies", "description": "For a thousand gold coins, a mother gave her grown daughter to a man dying on a stake. He wanted a son. After his death. 🪙\n\nLast tale's answer: Vikram said the thief was the only truly generous man. A husband cannot keep a wife whose heart is elsewhere. The friend let her go because his love had cooled with time, and he was afraid her husband, who knew everything, would tell the king. But the thief, a reckless man working in the dark, let go a lovely bride and all her gold.\n\nVikram & Betaal: A Bride for 1000 Gold Coins.\nThe parts we couldn't fit in the reel:\n\nDhanavati was the only child of Dhanapala, a very rich merchant of Tamralipti. Her mother was Hiranyavati. When her father died, she was a grown woman, and his relations seized his property.\n\nThe thief had one more request before he died: burn my body, throw my bones into sacred water, and go to the city of Vakrolaka, where a good king rules. Her mother did it all, and they lived there in a house bought with the thief's gold.\n\nThe scholar's name was Manahsvamin. He needed the five hundred gold coins for a courtesan named Hamsavali, and he had no money. He took the coins, stayed one night and left in secret next morning.\n\nThe old king was Suryaprabha, and he named the boy Chandraprabha. He named him his successor, then went to Varanasi as an old man, and died there.\n\nThe ministers begged the young king not to go on pilgrimage: a kingdom cannot stand unguarded for a moment, and the road has many dangers. He answered that the body perishes in a moment, and left them to guard the kingdom. He stopped at the Ganges, Prayag and Varanasi before he reached the well of Gaya.\n\nIn the book, the second hand holds a colander, used to filter soma juice. We show a palm-leaf book so the sign reads at once.\n\n(From Somadeva's Ocean of Story, the Vetala tales.)\n\nSo, whose son is he? The thief who gave him a name… the man who gave him blood… or the king who gave him a life? 👇\n\n#vikrambetaal #indianhorror #ghoststories #indianfolklore #horrorstories", "channel": "feartalkies", "uploader_id": "58803293522", "uploader": "Fear Talkies | Indian Horror", "timestamp": 1793511141, "like_count": 3451, "comment_count": 26, "http_headers": {"Referer": "https://www.instagram.com/"}, "formats": [{"format_id": "dash-1431780648934857a", "ext": "m4a", "tbr": 67.573, "asr": 44100, "format_note": "DASH audio", "container": "m4a_dash", "vcodec": "none", "acodec": "mp4a.40.5", "url": "https://scontent-ord5-1.cdninstagram.com/o1/v/t2/f2/m78/AQMRV9wJFRComRc0hK3i_4DJ2GDhBxLq4f17F1k41Y8a2hMfC8_XlKNAHJ5tmyLK6rPRjYX5pasg-Q2wt1yrNNJjnafw-j3LsB_6OXc.mp4?_nc_cat=101&_nc_sid=9ca052&_nc_ht=scontent-ord5-1.cdninstagram.com&_nc_ohc=k-h8Lt7m1Z0Q7kNvwG9cm2T&%3D%3D&ccb=17-1&_nc_gid=rwmkggCQOx0O_rOuYALgAg&_nc_ss=70689&_nc_zt=28&oh=00_AQR11SAwt7fALR1NdtjUz4KswloxJ49NC1SUohOLNwtP1A&oe=6AF3E1FE", "manifest_stream_number": 0, "is_dash_periods": true, "protocol": "https", "audio_ext": "m4a", "video_ext": "none", "vbr": 0, "abr": 67.573, "resolution": "audio only", "http_headers": {"User-Agent": "Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/146.0.0.0 Safari/537.36", "Accept": "text/html,application/xhtml+xml,application/xml;q=0.9,*/*;q=0.8", "Accept-Language": "en-us,en;q=0.5", "Sec-Fetch-Mode": "navigate", "Referer": "https://www.instagram.com/"}, "format": "dash-1431780648934857a - audio only (DASH audio)"}, {"url": "https://scontent-ord5-2.cdninstagram.com/o1/v/t2/f2/m86/AQOtC7IjZ6zE3bUnd-wa7GHoPgu0Xc7C4hjlaAHZf5lUWg1owVpJQA4n1Phd_kjA-mcaSTM8Hji74HzpgoZ7_uAkx--xjFLIUUtXfLg.mp4?_nc_cat=107&_nc_sid=5e9851&_nc_ht=scontent-ord5-2.cdninstagram.com&_nc_ohc=FdLbaJOUSgwQ7kNvwE3KV4O&efg=eyJ2ZW5jb2RlX3RhZyI6Inhwdl9wcm9ncmVzc2l2ZS5JTlNUQUdSQU0uQ0xJUFMuQzMuNzIwLmRhc2hfYmFzZWxpbmVfMV92MSIsInhwdl9hc3NldF9pZCI6MTQzMTc4MDQzODkzNDg3OCwiYXNzZXRfYWdlX2RheXMiOjgsInZpX3VzZWNhc2VfaWQiOjEwMDk5LCJkdXJhdGlvbl9zIjoxNzQsInV